# BEFORE THE ZENODO DEPOSIT, A HUMAN MUST REPLACE EVERY PLACEHOLDER BELOW.
# Nothing here may be guessed. A fabricated ORCID, affiliation, or email in a
# citation file is worse than a blank one, because it silently mis-attributes.
#
# The `orcid`, `email`, `date-released`, and `doi` keys are pattern-constrained
# by the CFF 1.2.0 schema, so a literal placeholder in them would make this file
# fail validation. They are therefore left COMMENTED OUT below. Uncomment each
# one as you fill it in. The file as it stands is schema-valid and honest about
# what it does not yet know.
#
#   ORCID-PENDING          -> the author's real ORCID iD, as a full URL, e.g.
#                             https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000
#                             If an author has no ORCID, delete their `orcid:`
#                             line entirely rather than inventing a value.
#   AFFILIATION-PENDING    -> the author's institution, exactly as it will read
#                             on the title page of the manuscript.
#   EMAIL-PENDING          -> the corresponding author's email address.
#   DOI-PENDING            -> the reserved Zenodo DOI (see
#                             docs/guides/ARTIFACT_DEPOSIT.md, step 2), added
#                             as an `identifiers:` entry and, after release, as
#                             the top-level `doi:` field.
#   VERSION-PENDING        -> the release tag, e.g. v1.0.0.
#   DATE-RELEASED-PENDING  -> the deposit date, as YYYY-MM-DD.
#
# The same placeholders exist in .zenodo.json; keep the two files in step.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Participation Is Not Collaboration: Tracing Public Ownership After
  Cross-Product Agent Review
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper and this
  software record.
