    # orcid: ORCID-PENDING   <- https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis artifact for a study of what happens after one coding
  agent reviews a pull request written by a different coding agent. The
  repository pins the AIDev-7.6M release, reconstructs the public event path
  from cross-product review to an exact addressed edge, a next visible owner,
  and a later merge state, and reports every robustness check and rejected
  claim. It contains the analysis and figure code, the reproduction contract,
  the tests, and the derived analysis products the manuscript tables and
  figures are built from. It does not redistribute the AIDev release, and it
  does not contain the private coder keys used by the blinded human-coding
  audits.
keywords:
  - mining software repositories
  - coding agents
  - agentic software engineering
  - code review
  - human-agent collaboration
  - pull requests
  - reproducibility artifact
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/technoob05/emse2026-multiagent-impact'
version: VERSION-PENDING
# date-released: DATE-RELEASED-PENDING   <- uncomment, as YYYY-MM-DD
# doi: DOI-PENDING                       <- the reserved Zenodo DOI
references:
  - type: data
    title: 'AIDev: Studying AI Coding Agents on GitHub'
    authors:
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Hao
    repository: 'https://huggingface.co/datasets/hao-li/AIDev-7.6M'
    notes: >-
